From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Standalone dispatch: omitted optional arguments keep their
 default

A script call that leaves out an argument (`LightSeq.Play SeqRandom, 50, ,
1000`) passes VT_ERROR/DISP_E_PARAMNOTFOUND in its slot. Since 8db5f784 the
generated Invoke proxies return conversion failures to the script, so that
marker now fails the call with a type mismatch instead of the parameter
keeping its [defaultvalue], as COM dispatch does.

The generator fetches every argument through one path: typed
[defaultvalue]/[optional] parameters map the marker to their default
(ArgOrDefault), optional VARIANT parameters still receive it, as their
methods expect, and a present argument that does not convert still fails
the call. An optional VARIANT* parameter left out entirely (a bare
`Debug.Print`) no longer reads before an empty argument array.
